--- body ---
## Context

Found by a /smelt run on sen-causal-reading (2026-11-07): the project has no
`memory/SMELT.md`, so `scripts/smelt_migrate.py` refuses with "Missing memory
consolidation prompt", and the harness ships no starter prompt
(`conception/memory-v8/templates/` has none).

An audit of every copy shows the per-project prompt is generic text copied,
not a real editorial layer:

| Project | File | Base | Local content |
|---|---|---|---|
| harness | memory/SMELT.md 10.1 KB | v8-r5 | journal sizes, size-script path, ticket 1349 |
| padme | memory/SMELT.md 6.3 KB | v8-r2 (as r3-padme1) | rules + native-store paths; re-encryption limited to topics so encrypted journal entries stay append-only |
| climate-finance-het | memory/DREAM.md 6.4 KB | v8-r1 | rules paths; 2026-10-14 native-notes import annex location |
| JETP-observer (+ arena/repos and .codex clones) | memory/DREAM.md 5.7 KB | v8-r1 | none (carries the temp-ciphertext fix later adopted upstream) |

Findings: (1) all project copies are 1–4 revisions stale: no topic job, no
4 KB cap, no attribution skip, while SKILL.md points into
"memory/SMELT.md § Job of a topic and caps" and "§ Rebuild" (dependency runs
the wrong way); (2) generic fixes made in one copy do not propagate (padme's
append-only clarification for encrypted journal entries is still implicit in
r5); (3) the only truly local facts are locations (rules, native store,
import annex). Overlaps ticket 1443 (memory redesign): this is a bounded
step inside it, not a competing redesign.

## Decision

Author authorised this work on 2026-11-07 on the recommended option:
**no per-project prompt**. All generic consolidation text lives in the smelt
skill (SKILL.md + references/); local facts become one or two lines in the
project's `memory/MEMORY.md` (or a SOURCES.md it links). Fallback if the
implementer finds a genuine editorial divergence: a thin optional
`memory/SMELT.md` holding only overrides, absent = defaults. Report the
revision of the skill (not of a project prompt) in each smelt report.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Generic content of `memory/SMELT.md` (Read, Rebuild, Job of a topic and caps, Consolidate, Coherence, Encrypted entries, Report, Bounds) lives in `skills/smelt/` with no duplication against SKILL.md; padme's append-only rule for encrypted journal entries is stated explicitly
- [ ] SKILL.md no longer depends on a project file for caps or the size helper; the size helper is invoked from `$IDH_ROOT`
- [ ] `scripts/smelt_migrate.py` treats a missing prompt as the default (no refusal); legacy DREAM.md/HOARD.md/SMELT.md copies are retired by the migration with their local location facts carried into the index; tests updated
- [ ] `conception/memory-v8/templates/` and live memory docs updated to match
- [ ] The harness's own `memory/SMELT.md` is retired (harness-only facts moved to its index/topics)
- [ ] One ticket filed in each of padme, JETP-observer, climate-finance-het to retire their copy on next smelt (cross-project: tickets only, no edits there)
- [ ] Log on ticket 1443 linking this ticket
- [ ] Harness gate passes

## Raid annotations (Imagine + Plan, raid 34342e, 2026-11-07)

Single-ticket raid; the orchestrator read the surfaces itself (cost: a
per-ticket Imagine fan-out buys nothing on a ticket whose option the author
has already chosen). Premise holds on origin/main 5971d810: SKILL.md cites
`memory/SMELT.md § Job of a topic and caps` and `§ Rebuild`;
`scripts/smelt_migrate.py:157` raises "Missing memory consolidation prompt".

Plan:
1. New `skills/smelt/references/` file(s) carrying the generic sections of
   harness `memory/SMELT.md` v8-r5 (Read + blob ledger, Rebuild by department,
   Job of a topic and caps, departments list, Consolidate, Coherence,
   Encrypted entries with key scheme and three failure modes, Report, Bounds).
   SKILL.md keeps the contract and points into the reference; no paragraph
   stated in both. Encrypted entries: state padme's r3-padme1 rule
   explicitly — re-encryption applies to consolidated pages under
   `memory/topics/` only; an encrypted journal entry is read, never rewritten.
2. Size helper invoked as `python3 "$IDH_ROOT/scripts/memory_sizes.py"`
   against the selected project (check it accepts a project root; add the
   argument if not, test first).
3. Report names the skill revision (a revision line in the skill, or the
   harness commit of `skills/smelt/`), not a project prompt revision.
4. `smelt_migrate.py`: no prompt = defaults, no refusal. A legacy
   DREAM.md/HOARD.md/SMELT.md is retired by the migration; its local location
   facts (rules paths, native-store or import-annex locations) reach the
   index. The helper cannot judge which lines are local: preferred shape is
   that the helper retires the file and reports it, and the skill's
   migration step tells the agent to carry the local location facts into
   `memory/MEMORY.md` (≤40 lines) or a linked SOURCES.md before committing.
   Optional thin `memory/SMELT.md` of overrides only if a genuine editorial
   divergence is found (none known: padme's divergence is now generic).
5. Templates (`conception/memory-v8/templates/`), `conception/memory-v8/*.md`
   live docs, `skills/lair/SKILL.md`, tests (`test_smelt_migrate.py`,
   `test_dream_v8.py`, `test_skill_seam.py`, `test_memory_v8_*`) updated.
6. Harness `memory/SMELT.md` retired; harness-only facts (journal sizes
   2026-10-29, departments provisional until ticket 1349) move to the index
   or `memory/topics/memory-v8-governance.md`.
7. Cross-project tickets (padme, JETP-observer, climate-finance-het) and the
   1443 log line: filed by the orchestrator, not the executor.
